NAME
       vt_switch, vt_set_ctty, vt_spawn_poll - virtual consoles

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/cervus.h>

       int cervus_vt_switch(int n);
       int cervus_vt_set_ctty(int n);
       int cervus_vt_spawn_poll(void);
       int cervus_vt_clear_shell(int n);

DESCRIPTION
       The console is a set of virtual terminals, each with its own
       grid, cursor and attributes. Ctrl-Alt-F1 through F12 switch
       between them from the keyboard; vt_switch does the same from a
       program.

       One of the terminals is the kernel debug monitor rather than a
       shell.

       init calls vt_spawn_poll to learn which terminals have been
       asked for a shell but do not have one yet, and vt_set_ctty to
       make a terminal the controlling one for the shell it starts
       there.

       Terminal contents survive a font change: the grid is reflowed to
       the new cell size and the cursor moved to match.

RETURN VALUE
       0 or a terminal number on success, negative on failure.

SEE ALSO
       setfont(2), openpty(2), init(1)
